<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Omsk is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irtysh">Irtysh</a> and Om rivers. Founded as a fortress in 1716, it became the administrative centre of the Steppe region. In 1918–1919 it was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kolchak">Admiral Kolchak</a>'s White government, and it is now a major industrial city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omsk.jpg" alt="Omsk" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Крылов Иван, Siberiano, PetarM, LittleDrakon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omsk_Collage_2016.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
